WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.030
Water: one oxygen atom and two hydrogens.

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:08.010
Carbon dioxide: one carbon
atom and two oxygens.

3
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.590
Three atoms each.

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.850
Yet water is bent, and carbon
dioxide is perfectly straight.

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.670
So why is one bent and the other straight?

6
00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.590
In this mission, you'll count the
electron domains around a central atom,

7
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.650
and use them to predict the shape of a
molecule and the angles between its bonds.

8
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.030
You'll tell electron-domain
geometry from molecular geometry,

9
00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.570
and see what sets the
angles between bonds.

10
00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:37.490
Your mission: explain why water is
bent but carbon dioxide is straight.
